$blocked$;

-- Proposed permission core, NOT a complete/final security boundary:
REVOKE ALL PRIVILEGES ON TABLE public.conversations, public.messages,
    public.user_ai_integrations FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;
GRANT SELECT ON TABLE public.conversations, public.messages TO authenticated;

-- REQUIRED BEFORE FINALIZATION:
-- 1. Inventory and explicitly revoke independent column privileges; inspect
--    effective inherited privileges, role attributes and schema privileges.
--    REVOKE at table level alone does not remove column/inherited grants.
-- 2. Review every policy expression, mode, name and role. Remove unsupported
--    browser DML policies; retain authenticated own-row reads. Add mandatory
--    ownership/parent checks where warranted, without assuming unknown policies.
--    Anonymous access stays denied; integration access stays backend-only.
-- 3. Audit exposed views, write RPCs/SECURITY DEFINER functions and their grants:
--    table revocations do not prevent writes through privileged functions.
-- 4. Verify the actual backend role retains required privileges. Do not rewrite
--    Auth schema grants or assume RLS constrains service_role/BYPASSRLS.
-- 5. Assert effective browser DML/TRUNCATE/TRIGGER/REFERENCES and all integration
--    privileges are denied, including column grants; assert own reads still work.
-- 6. No UPDATE/DELETE/backfill of application records belongs in this migration.
--    Keep all legacy NULL-owned records. No FK, trigger or deletion-rule changes.
-- Missing canonical catalog evidence blocks the final policy/privilege SQL.

ROLLBACK; -- Even deliberate guard removal must not accidentally apply a draft.
